    <div class="about-mid-text">
      <h2 class="about-section-heading">Listening to the Land Through Art</h2>
      <p>I didn't set out to become a conservation minded artist. I set out to paint the land that raised me. Another aspect of my art is to bring awareness to care for our natural world and the planet that we call home.</p>
      <p>Growing up in the Pacific Northwest, I spent most of my life exploring many of the natural places that the land has to offer. Having that privilege is the sole driving force behind my passion for conservation efforts through art.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="about-img-pair">
    <img src="/assets/about/daina-lakeside.jpg" alt="Daina sitting by the water">
    <img src="/assets/about/daina-winter-river.jpg" alt="Daina exploring a winter river landscape">
  </div>

  <p>Raven and Cedar Studio got its name from this very concept and my intention is to reach other voices who share the same passion and activism that I do to fight for our natural world through creative expression.</p>

  <div class="about-closing">
    <div class="about-closing-text">
      <p>As a mother and a caretaker I find it deeply important to not only be a steward of the land but to share that voice with the generations that follow. One day, this is what I will leave my children and I want to leave them with the same natural beauty that has inspired me so.</p>
